    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's what I implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\nThe task required returning a human-formatted `telephoneDisplay` field alongside the raw E.164 `telephone`. `OwnerDto` is generated from `openapi.yml` at build time, and the response is produced by `OwnerMapper`, so the change spans three files:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `telephoneDisplay` property (read-only, derived) to the `Owner` schema so the generated DTO carries the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerTelephone.java`** \u2014 Added a `toDisplay(e164)` helper that identifies the country calling code from the existing `NATIONAL_LENGTH` codes and formats the number as `+<code> <national digits grouped in threes>` (e.g. `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`). Made the class/method `public` so the mapper (a different package) can reuse this single source of truth for the telephone rule. Non-E.164 or unknown-code values are returned unchanged.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Wired a `@Named(\"telephoneDisplay\")` mapping that calls `OwnerTelephone.toDisplay(owner.getTelephone())`, keeping `telephone` as the stored raw E.164.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` passes, confirming `telephone` stays `+61412345678` while `telephoneDisplay` is `+61 412 345 678`, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).",
